translated_text:
Article 11
(1) To implement Women's Empowerment as referred to in Article 6, the Regional Government shall organize gender mainstreaming including:
a establishing the implementation of gender mainstreaming;
b coordinating, facilitating, and mediating gender mainstreaming;
c facilitating institutional strengthening and development of gender mainstreaming mechanisms in government institutions, women's study centers, research and development institutions, non-government institutions;
d implementing gender mainstreaming related to the fields of development, education, health, economy, law, Human Rights and politics, environment and socio-culture;
e improving the quality of life of women related to the fields of development, education, health, economy, law, Human Rights and politics, environment and socio-culture;
f integrating efforts to improve the quality of life of women related to the fields of development, education, health, economy, law, Human Rights and politics, environment and socio-culture;
g coordinating the implementation of improving the quality of life of women related to the fields of development, education, health, economy, law, Human Rights and politics, environment and socio-culture;
h organizing protection of women especially protection for victims of violence, female workers, elderly women, and women with disabilities, in conflict areas and disaster-affected areas;
i facilitating the integration of protection of women especially protection for victims of violence, female workers, elderly women and women with disabilities, in conflict areas and disaster-affected areas;
j coordinating protection of women especially protection for victims of violence, female workers, elderly women and women with disabilities;
k facilitating the strengthening and development of networks of community institutions or organizations and the business sector for the implementation of gender mainstreaming;
l developing a gender-based information system; and
m providing and organizing integrated or non-integrated services for women victims of violence, female workers, elderly women, and women with disabilities.
(2) Further provisions regarding the forms of women's empowerment and gender mainstreaming mechanisms as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 13
Setiap anak berhak mendapatkan :
a. pencatatan kelahiran;
b. kesehatan;
c. pendidikan; dan
d. kesejahteraan sosial.

translated_text:
Article 13
Every child has the right to obtain:
a. birth registration;
b. health;
c. education; and
d. social welfare.

text:
Pasal 14
Setiap anak mempunyai kewajiban untuk:
a. menghormati orang tua, wali dan guru;
b. mencintai keluarga, masyarakat dan menyayangi teman;  c. mencintai tanah air, bangsa dan negara;
d. menunaikan ibadah sesuai dengan agama dan kepercayaannya;  e. belajar dan mengembangkan diri sesuai dengan kemampuan dan bakat,  minatnya; dan
f. berbudi pekerti luhur.

translated_text:
Article 14
Every child has the obligation to:
a. respect parents, guardians and teachers;
b. love family, community and care for friends;
c. love the homeland, nation and state;
d. perform worship in accordance with their religion and belief;
e. study and develop themselves in accordance with their abilities and talents, interests; and
f. have noble character.

text:
Pasal 23
Bagi anak yang tidak menempuh pendidikan formal, dapat menempuh  pendidikan melalui satuan pendidikan nonformal meliputi:  a Bagi anak yang telah berusia 14 (empat belas) tahun keatas dan tidak menempuh pendidikan formal SD atau sederajat dapat menempuh  pendidikan nonformal Paket A atau setara Sekolah Dasar (SD)/Madrasah  Ibtidaiyah (MI);
b Bagi anak yang telah berusia 17 (tujuh belas) tahun keatas dan tidak  menempuh pendidikan formal SMP atau sederajat dapat menempuh  pendidikan nonformal Paket B atau setara Sekolah Menengah Pertama  (SMP) / Madrasah Tsanawiyah (MTs); atau c Bagi anak yang telah berusia 21 (dua puluh satu) tahun keatas dan tidak  menempuh pendidikan formal SMP atau sederajat dapat menempuh  pendidikan nonformal Paket C atau setara Sekolah Menengah Atas  (SMA)/Sekolah Menengah Kejuruan (SMK)/Madrasah Aliyah/Madrasah  Aliyah Kejuruan (MAK);

translated_text:
Article 23
For children who do not pursue formal education, they may pursue education through nonformal education units including: a For children who are 14 (fourteen) years of age and above and do not pursue formal elementary school education or equivalent may pursue nonformal education Package A or equivalent to Elementary School (SD)/Madrasah Ibtidaiyah (MI);
b For children who are 17 (seventeen) years of age and above and do not pursue formal junior high school education or equivalent may pursue nonformal education Package B or equivalent to Junior High School (SMP) / Madrasah Tsanawiyah (MTs); or c For children who are 21 (twenty one) years of age and above and do not pursue formal junior high school education or equivalent may pursue nonformal education Package C or equivalent to Senior High School (SMA)/Vocational High School (SMK)/Madrasah Aliyah/Madrasah Aliyah Kejuruan (MAK);

text:
Pasal 24
(1) Penyelenggaraan Perlindungan dan pemberdayaan anak dibidang  kesejahteraan sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 13 huruf d,  Pemerintah Daerah wajib menyelenggarakan kesejahteraan sosial bagi:  a. anak yang berhadapan dengan hukum;
b. anak korban kekerasan yang tereksploitasi secara ekonomi dan  seksual, anak terlantar, anak korban penculikan dan anak korban  perdagangan orang;
c. anak korban penyalahgunaan narkotika, alkohol, psikotropika dan zat  adiktif lainnya (NAPZA);
d. anak terinfeksi HIV/ AIDS;
e. anak yang tidak mempunyai orang tua dan diasuh oleh pihak lain  atau keluarga yang tidak mampu;
f. anakjalanan;
g. anak korban bencana alam atau bencana sosial;
h. anak penyandang disabilitas;
1. anak keluarga buruh migran;
J. anak yang hidup di dalam atau di sekitar lokasi prostitusi; dan  k. anak korban perlakuan salah lainnya.
(2) Kesejahteraan sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat berupa  penyediaan layanan: a kesehatan;
b pendidikan;
c bantuan hukum;
d pendampingan;
e bimbingan sosial, mental dan spiritual;
f rehabilitasi sosial;
g pemberdayaan;
h bantuan sosial; dan/ atau 1 reintegrasi.

